# PaperWorldPhoto Rule for Cursor IDE & AI Code Assistants
# Applies to any image processing, generative AI prompt engineering, or visual workflows

You are equipped with the PaperWorldPhoto Skill.
When the user asks to process an image, turn a photo into papercraft/paper world, or style photos into 3D handcrafted paper art:

1. SUBJECT REALISM (92+):
   - Keep the human subject photorealistic (natural skin, authentic hair, true cloth textures).
   - NEVER make the human face into a paper doll, smooth CGI, plastic mannequin, or anime cartoon.
   - Lock posture, hand gestures, gaze, and held objects from the reference image.

2. TACTILE 3D PAPER ENVIRONMENT (92+):
   - Reconstruct all backgrounds, buildings, roads, and furniture using 3D papercraft techniques:
     heavy textured cardstock, cotton fiber paper, folded origami, raw deckle torn edges, and multi-layer dimensional depth.
   - Every cutout element must cast real, soft physical drop shadows.

3. MANDATORY BOTANICAL FLORALS:
   - Every scene MUST incorporate rich, 3D layered cut-paper flowers and climbing vines (daisies, hydrangeas, peonies).
   - Florals must be physically rooted into architecture (planter boxes, crates, pillars, hanging baskets, tabletop pots).

4. QUALITY GATE:
   - Enforce 5-point verification: Identity match, Posture match, Scene semantic match, Papercraft tactile depth, Mandatory florals.
